<Base
  title="About"
  description="Every Share Votes is an independent shareholder project by Jason Crawford. Not affiliated with Tesla or SpaceX. Not investment advice."
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this project</p>
    <h1>Independent shareholder project.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Not affiliated with Tesla or SpaceX. Not investment advice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every Share Votes is maintained by Jason Crawford, an independent retail shareholder. He is
      not an officer, director, employee, or agent of Tesla, Inc. or SpaceX, and he does not speak
      for either company. The site uses “TSLA” for the stock. It uses the company name when a filing
      or a statute uses it. The name and the check-mark logo are not the companies’ marks.
    </p>
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>A plain-English reading of public filings about a possible combination.</li>
      <li>A map to the company’s own voting instructions and retail voting program.</li>
      <li>A table of Form 13F positions, generated from the SEC’s quarterly data set.</li>
      <li>A voting-history table that leaves a cell blank of any number unless a filing or a press report is linked.</li>
      <li>A self-reported share ledger, labeled unverified, plus a sentiment chart that leaves missing series empty.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>Not a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold, and not a recommendation to vote for or against anything.</li>
      <li>Not a proxy solicitation. If a proxy is filed, read that proxy.</li>
      <li>Not legal advice about Texas law or about any account’s voting rights.</li>
      <li>Not a complete list of shareholders. Form 13F misses retail holders, many non-U.S. holders, and insider forms.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How the 13F file is made</h2>
    <p>
      <code>scripts/fetch_13f.py</code> reads the newest ZIP on the SEC’s
      <a href="https://www.sec.gov/data-research/sec-markets-data/form-13f-data-sets">Form 13F data sets</a>
      page, keeps CUSIP 88160R101, drops put and call rows, and keeps the latest 13F-HR or amendment
      for each manager and report period. The script sends a User-Agent with a contact address and
      waits between requests. A weekly GitHub Action runs the same script and opens a pull request
      when the JSON changes. Set the repository secret <code>SEC_CONTACT_EMAIL</code> to a mailbox
      a person monitors.
    </p>
    <h2>How the tally is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Pages runs <code>functions/api/shares.ts</code> against a D1 database bound as
      <code>DB</code>. The ledger schema is <code>migrations/0002_share_ledger.sql</code>. Nothing is seeded.
      The rules are on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page. If the binding, the hash salt, or Turnstile is missing, the page says so and does not show a made-up zero.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      A number on this site should have a source link and a date. If a filing is amended, the page
      should follow the amendment. Institutional vote cells stay “Not found” until someone links the
      N-PX filing or a report that states the vote.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
